{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/756956-are-battlegroups-worth-the-investment-for-a-solar","id":756956,"title":"Are Battlegroups worth the investment for a Solar?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-05T11:19:01-08:00","id":756956,"title":"Are Battlegroups worth the investment for a Solar?","content":"Hi! First time posting on this board. I have recently started digging through the PDF and am really keen to start playing! In 2nd ED games I enjoyed playing a Solar General, heavily investing in backgrounds like Followers and Allies to represent my growing army and its loyal officers. While this made for some great roleplay and was often useful on a strategic level, due to the nature of 2nd ed my poor mortal buddies were largely irrelevant the moment any serious conflict broke out. The advent of battlegroups has given me hope that my trusty legionnaires can be more than just stunt fodder this time around!<br /> <br /> My question is, am I right to be optimistic? Can it be effective/noteworthy to bring a battlegroup with you? I am currently looking at picking up say Command 3. Will they be quickly made irrelevant against solar level threats? Any tips, tricks or charms I should look into to make my plucky mortals more effective? Is it worth taking War Supernal on my Zenith? (It seems to be an oddly short tree at first glance, so dubious right now).<br /> <br /> I have only been looking through the book for a few days, so all advice (no matter how obvious it might seem) is welcome!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:34:43-08:00","id":756993,"title":"","content":"&quot;Solar level&quot; threats can shred battle groups pretty fast especially with the right Charms. <br /> <br /> However the vast majority of threats should not at all be &quot;Solar level.&quot; Tiger Warriors are going to destroy an unaugmented enemy mortal army, for example. A force of Tiger Warriors will probably do some damage to DBs and demons. Etc. <br /> <br /> And if you and your army go up against a &quot;Soler level&quot; foe, you and your Circlemates should be stepping up to face it, not your mortal army!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:44:15-08:00","id":757000,"title":"","content":"Yeah, &quot;Solar level threats&quot; was probably hyperbole on my part, I was more thinking 'things with essence pools' I suppose. Eh, I enjoy it anyway, so I figure I will roll with command 3 and see how things go!<br /> <br /> Still not sure if I should go with Presence or War as supernal, will just have to go through the charms with a fine tooth comb. Any advice on good things to do with battlegroups is still welcome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:49:50-08:00","id":757034,"title":"","content":"Just running some quick numbers on the Magnitude 3 version of Command 3, it's pretty sweet. 10 dice on the attack (8 with the spear), 15 base damage, 10 soak, and a parry of 6. That's &quot;you better be a dedicated fighter&quot; levels of danger, and all those pools can be boosted by you taking the command action, which you'll probably be good at as a Solar general. Add in that your battle group can attack over a very wide area each turn since it's about a hundred men, and it has ten health levels that yeah, all attacks target, but you can effectively &quot;heal&quot; in combat time with the rally for numbers action, and yeah they'll be useful. Don't feed them into the meat grinder against a dedicated Dawn caste swords man if you want to bring some of them home, but against mortals, Wyld barbarians, the odd first circle demon, yeah they'll be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1398-corwin859","name":"corwin859","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T12:00:00-08:00","id":757043,"title":"","content":"IMO Presence is a better Supernal choice simply because social interaction is more likely to come up than mass combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T12:20:19-08:00","id":757091,"title":"","content":"Depends on the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}